**Analysis:** By selectively stripping hydrogen out of the reaction zone, the localized partial pressure of H2 drops, triggering Le Chatelier's principle and driving the endothermic equilibrium (dH = +45.92 kJ/mol) forward. The **Jiang 2021 Target** case (SMA = 4.5 cm2/g vs 0.33 cm2/g baseline) demonstrates that a 13.6x increase in specific membrane area elevates conversion by {{ "%0.2f"|format(results_b['Jiang 2021 Target']['Gain_X']) }} percentage points and recovers {{ "%0.2f"|format(results_b['Jiang 2021 Target']['HRF']) }}% of the produced hydrogen as ultra-pure permeate.

